THE COMMENT THIS WAVE MADE FALSE IS REWRITTEN WITHOUT AN ERRATUM: the rule is kept (a second meaning on one activation of one element is a new interaction contract, not a reuse) and the contract is stated as two gestures. fisc-ppkq's notes are corrected in the same session.

MEASURED, and two of them contradict this bead:
  all 44 views the chain opens draw THREE columns at the page's own budget and one draws four at a four-column budget -- none draws two, so the 'a page with a drill has two drawn tiers, and isolating says almost nothing' premise the one-gesture design rested on is gone;
  24 of the 343 marks those views draw open, so the single click was carrying one meaning for 7% of an opened chart and another for 93%;
  over the overview and those 44 views, 368 marks: 44 carry the triangle, 17 the diamond alone, 0 carry both -- the composed marker is latent and pinned at zero;
  9 of the 44 views draw an aggregate.

TWO OF THIS BEAD'S OWN INSTRUCTIONS WERE MEASURED WRONG AND NOT FOLLOWED.
  'style.css:664-666 moves cursor:pointer OFF svg.sankey .node onto .node.opens -- today every node claims to be clickable and most are not.' FALSE. Every node is clickable: a click isolates it, and after this change every node's single click does the same thing. The pointer stays on svg.sankey .node and the stylesheet now carries the measurement. The distinction the owner asked for is the marker, which is a channel the cursor has not got.
  'nodeClass gains expands (isAggregate(d.id))' with a marker and a cursor. NOT DONE, because nothing in app.js can expand an aggregate until fisc-ko1j.12.6 lands -- it would be a promise broken on nine charts, which is this bead's own first sentence applied to itself. nodeClass's doc comment records that and names the bead; fisc-ko1j.12.6's notes now carry everything it owes, including that the gesture branches are already there to hang it on.

THE CHECKS COULD NOT BE WRITTEN THE WAY THIS BEAD SPELLS THEM, and that is the lane's third instance of the same trap. MEASURED: D3.select("#chart").size() is 0 in tools/jscheck, .append("g") returns a size-0 selection, and an .attr() accessor is invoked ZERO times -- so there is no .opens to count in a DOM, no <g> to dispatch a keydown at, and a handler written inline on that selection executes in no check. The three gestures are named functions for that reason alone, and GESTURE_WIRING pins as text the seven lines of render() that use them. Filed as fisc-xsc8 with what it would take to close, and with why planting #chart is the trap rather than the fix.

FOUR ARMS, EACH MUTATION RUN AND REVERTED:
